From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 15:40:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: allow disabling WoWLAN capability registration

Some configurations use the normal PCI and firmware suspend path
throughout. Allow the kernel configuration to omit WoWLAN capability
registration, which also makes cfg80211 reject a request to enable it.
The default preserves the existing capability for other builds.

Codex checked the ath12k capability registration and nl80211 trigger
validation, and added the build switch for the Piano NixOS kernel.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/Kconfig | 8 ++++++++
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wow.c   | 3 ++-
 2 files changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/Kconfig b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/Kconfig
index 0d5d1c55b..18198134a 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/Kconfig
@@ -14,6 +14,14 @@ config ATH12K
 
 	  If you choose to build a module, it'll be called ath12k.
 
+config ATH12K_WOWLAN
+	bool "ath12k Wake on Wireless LAN"
+	depends on ATH12K && PM
+	default y
+	help
+	  Advertise Wake on Wireless LAN when supported by the firmware.
+	  Turning this off keeps the normal suspend and resume path.
+
 config ATH12K_AHB
 	bool "Qualcomm ath12k AHB support"
 	depends on ATH12K && REMOTEPROC
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wow.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wow.c
index d8789104d..47c56f592 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wow.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/wow.c
@@ -1023,7 +1023,8 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL(ath12k_wow_op_resume);
 
 int ath12k_wow_init(struct ath12k *ar)
 {
-	if (!test_bit(WMI_TLV_SERVICE_WOW, ar->wmi->wmi_ab->svc_map))
+	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ATH12K_WOWLAN) ||
+	    !test_bit(WMI_TLV_SERVICE_WOW, ar->wmi->wmi_ab->svc_map))
 		return 0;
 
 	ar->wow.wowlan_support = ath12k_wowlan_support;
